  "chapter": {
    "label": "Every screen",
    "heading": "216 phone screens and 170 desktop pages",
    "body": [
      "Every page of the Pro Figma file was scanned on 27 September 2026 and every screen-sized frame exported: phone screens at 390 points, desktop pages at 1,440 pixels. The four app pages hold 129 frames and the four web pages 167 desktop frames; shown once each, with the web’s own phone layouts and the Updates page added, that makes 216 phone screens and 170 desktop pages. Both indexes follow the dealer: sign-in, the auction list and a car’s detail, then the orders a win opens (negotiation, pre-payment, settlement and proof of payment, title and delivery), then the account, bank accounts, wallet and help.",
      "Most of the web pages’ phone frames copy the app’s and are shown once; the 42 that differ, with dollar prices, real Privacy, About and Help copy, empty states and a share sheet, are under Mobile web. The Redesign tabs hold the Updates page: a rebuilt car detail with a defects map, sign-in by phone number and loading states; the App Store sizes and the auction-card Explorations have tabs of their own. Sample emails, phone numbers and the sample portrait are masked, and so is the bank-transfer screenshot used as a sample proof of payment."
    ],
    "appCaption": "Every screen at phone width: the app flow by flow, then the web’s own phone layouts and the redesigns; open any screen to see all of it.",
    "webCaption": "Every desktop page, flow by flow; open any page to see all of it."
  },
